      "If a client pays you through an app, it's tempting to treat the invoice as optional — the money already landed, so why send a bill? Because the payment and the invoice do two different jobs: the app moves the money, the invoice is the record that proves what the money was for. This guide covers why you still invoice when you're paid by app, the friends-and-family trap that quietly costs freelancers buyer protection and clean books, how the 2026 1099-K reversal means most app payments now generate no IRS form at all — making your own invoices the only record of income you still owe tax on — which app fits which client, and the payment-instructions block that gets app-paid invoices paid on the first try.",
