        q: "Do I legally have to put my home address on an invoice?",
        a: "For most U.S. freelancers — sole proprietors and single-member LLCs billing for services — no. There's no general law requiring a residential address (or any physical address) on a service invoice. An invoice must identify you, the client, what's owed, and how to pay; your home address isn't part of that. Narrow exceptions exist (sales-tax permits, customs commercial invoices, LLC public filings), but those call for a business address, not specifically your home.",
