        a: "A common rule of thumb is to move 25–30% of every client payment into a separate tax savings account as it comes in. Because no taxes are withheld from freelance income and you'll owe both income tax and the roughly 15.3% self-employment tax, that set-aside is what makes quarterly estimated taxes a simple transfer instead of a surprise bill. Your income tracking tells you exactly what you earned each quarter, which is the number the estimate is built on.",
