        a: "Keep a complete record of your income (ideally a numbered invoice for every payment, so it reconciles against your 1099s) and your expenses (your business-account statement plus a photo of any paper receipt that matters, filed in one consistent folder). In an audit, an undocumented deduction is a disallowed one, so the receipt is what turns a write-off from a nervous guess into a defensible number. You don't need anything elaborate — just enough to prove what you earned and what you spent on the business.",
