        q: "Why do accounts payable departments reject invoices?",
        a: "The most common reasons are a missing or wrong purchase order (PO) number, vendor details that don't match the company's records, a failed three-way match (the invoice doesn't agree with the PO and the receipt), a duplicate or reused invoice number, math/tax errors, or the invoice being sent somewhere other than the AP inbox or portal. Many AP systems reject these automatically, sometimes without notifying the vendor.",
